Descripton
The project focuses on designing and developing a  Woodcraf Business Database that will store, organize, and manage essental business data. This includes product details, customer informaton, orders, and sales records. The database aims to improve data organizaton, ensure accuracy, and make informaton easily accessible for future system development. It serves as the foundaton for a potental business management system.

Key Functonalite
- Store and manage product informaton (woodcraf items) Record customer details 
- Track orders and sales transactons 
- Update and delete records when needed 
- Search and retrieve data efciently 
- Maintain data consistency and organizaton

Stakeholders
- Business Owner – Uses data for monitoring sales and inventory 
- Staf/Encoder – Inputs and updates data in the database 
- Customers – Source of order and transacton data 
- Database Developer (Project Team) – Designs and manages the database 
- Instructor – Evaluates the database design and implementaton

Core Data Process
1. Input – Data such as products, customers, and orders are entered into the database 
2. Processing – The database organizes and validates the data relatonships 
3. Storage – Data is stored in structured tables (e.g., products, customers, orders) 
4. Retrieval – Users can search and access stored data when needed 
5. Update/Delete – Records can be modifed or removed to maintain accuracy
